      "size": [
        590,
        350
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 8,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note about this Workflow",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Tile Test Workflow\n\nThis workflow runs the same process as the VL upscale nodes, with each stage as its own node. Use it to find and fix a problem in one area of an image, or to run a full upscale.\n\n### Nodes\n\n1. **Tile Test: Layout** solves the tile grid and draws it over your image, with each tile's number, row and column.\n2. **Tile Test: Upscale** runs the upscale model. Skip it for an image that is already upscaled, with `upscale_by` at 1.0.\n3. **Tile Test: Settings** outputs the values of one preset from the settings file.\n4. **Tile Test: Captions** writes the text for each tile and shows each step the VL model took to write it.\n5. **Tile Test: Render** refines the tiles you name, or the entire image.\n\n### Fixing a problem area\n\n1. Find the tile number over the problem area in the Layout preview.\n2. Enter that number in `tiles` on the Captions node. Its `tiles` output passes the number to Render.\n3. Read the Captions outputs to see what the VL model wrote for that tile.\n4. Change a setting or a wording, then render the tile again to compare.\n\nTurn on `with_neighbors` on both nodes to render the tile together with its bordering tiles, which is closer to the full run. The seed is only on the Render node, so a new seed reuses the upscale and the captions from the cache.\n\n### Full upscale\n\nLeave `tiles` empty on the Captions node to caption every tile. Render then refines the entire image."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Tile Test Workflow\n\nThis workflow runs the same process as the VL upscale nodes, with each stage as its own node. Use it to find and fix a problem in one area of an image, or to run a full upscale.\n\n### Nodes\n\n1. **Tile Test: Layout** solves the tile grid and draws it over your image, with each tile's number, row and column.\n2. **Tile Test: Upscale** runs the upscale model. Skip it for an image that is already upscaled, with `upscale_by` at 1.0.\n3. **Tile Test: Settings** outputs the values of one preset from the settings file.\n4. **Tile Test: Captions** writes the text for each tile and shows each step the VL model took to write it.\n5. **Tile Test: Render** refines the tiles you name, or the entire image.\n\n### Fixing a problem area\n\n1. Find the tile number over the problem area in the Layout preview.\n2. Enter that number in `tiles` on the Captions node. Its `tiles` output passes the number to Render.\n3. Read the Captions outputs to see what the VL model wrote for that tile.\n4. Change a setting or a wording, then render the tile again to compare.\n\nTurn on `with_neighbors` on both nodes to render the tile together with its bordering tiles, which is closer to the full run. The seed is only on the Render node, so a new seed reuses the upscale and the captions from the cache.\n\n### Full upscale\n\nLeave `tiles` empty on the Captions node to caption every tile. Render then refines the entire image."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
